        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "SATURDAY DECEMBER 30  Songwriting Workshop at Lacey Timberland Library  https://timberland/events  500 College St SE  Lacey, WA 98503  3 - 4:30 pm    Songcatchers: An Intergenerational Songwriting Workshop. A truly all-ages Creative Writing workshop with professional songwriter Keeth Apgar.    Elders are invited to co-create an original song from scratch alongside youth and families from within the community.    As we dig into the creative process, the group works with music concepts such as rhythm, melody, tempo and chords. We also touch upon the role of vowel sounds; discuss song structure, storytelling and creating images with words; dip into music theory; and develop listening skills. Time permitting we record a live version of our co- created original work.    Prior musical training is welcome although not necessary."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Songwriting Workshop at Lacey Timberland Library"
      }
    ],
