    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "July 25  |  August 1  |  August 8  |  August 15  Songwriting Series in Occidental Square  Hosted by Downtown Seattle Association  downtownseattle.org    Occidental Square  117 S. Washington St.  Seattle, WA 98104  1 - 3 pm    This will be a four-part songwriting series taking place on the following dates:    July 25  August 1  August 8  August 15    &nbsp;    Write a Song in the Park – A Community Songwriting Workshop with Keeth Apgar    In this unique and inclusive workshop, everyone is a songwriter.    Led by professional musician and teaching artist Keeth Apgar, this is a drop-in creative writing and music-making session where we’ll build an original song from scratch — using your ideas, your words, and your creativity.    Along the way, we’ll explore the elements of songwriting: rhythm, melody, harmony, and the magic of lyric writing. We’ll play with sounds and images, discuss what to do when you feel stuck, and talk about how to actually finish a song.    No musical background is needed — just a willingness to jump in and have fun.    This is folk art at its core — blending storytelling with music, and welcoming all voices to the circle. We’ll wrap up the workshop with a live recording of the song we write together.    🎤 All ages, all levels — no experience needed  📍 Just walk up and join us in the park!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Songwriting Series in Occidental Square (Downtown Seattle)"
      }
    ],
